# shadcn/ui & Styling Conventions

## Component Usage

- Use components from `@/components/ui/`
- Install new components with `npx shadcn@latest add [component-name]`
- Always use the `cn()` utility from `@/lib/utils` for merging Tailwind classes
- Configuration: `rsc: false` (Inertia SPA model, not React Server Components)
- Lucide React for all icons
- Compose shadcn primitives over raw HTML whenever a component exists

## Theming

- Dark mode as default with light mode toggle
- One global theme file for all frontend styling (font sizes, color palette, design tokens)
- CSS variables for theming (colors, radius, spacing)
- Consistent use of design tokens — never hardcode colors or sizes inline

## Accessibility

- `tabindex` on custom interactive elements
- `aria-label` on icon-only buttons and non-obvious controls
- Keyboard handlers (onKeyDown) alongside click handlers on interactive elements
- Semantic HTML elements (button for actions, a for navigation)
- Proper focus management on modals and overlays

## Responsive Design

- All components must be fully responsive
- Mobile-first approach with Tailwind breakpoints
- Test layouts at common breakpoints (sm, md, lg, xl)
